  "notes": "An announced card, with no result for any match; every name on it is filed as billed. In the page's running order: Trent Populi against Markus Tobin (the fed's own sheet for Deacon gives Trent Populi as the former jobber renamed Deacon, so the billing is read as Deacon's earlier name); Alexander Locksmith and Joel Alvereze against the Turks (Laguna and Reno); Joe Average against Ein, with Serenity; a triple threat of Guy Boudreaux, C.D. Justice and Paul St. Thomas (the sheet for Abraham gives Paul St. Thomas as the jobber renamed Abraham); Cleveland Paige against Arizona; and, in the main event, Chris Storm against 'Cool' Stevie Nash. The fed's concept page puts its shows in the Mid-South Coliseum in Tennessee and its news item names WREG Channel 3, both in-fiction places; neither is given as this card's venue."
